    <serviceCategories>
      <Value><![CDATA[[
  {
    "key": "e54ed150-83c9-4790-aba3-34d7b01e9dad",
    "name": "Item 1",
    "ncContentTypeAlias": "products",
    "categoryNumber": "01",
    "categoryHeading1": "Foundation investigations",
    "categoryHeading2": "investigations",
    "category": "<p>A foundation investigation involves assessing a building’s supporting foundations and identifying the causes of settlement and how best to rectify the problem.</p>",
    "categoryImage": "umb://media/63e6d7463e814dbe89a11c4eb4e3fd07"
  },
  {
    "key": "5793d463-aea4-4b09-acbc-2d7c0f088076",
    "name": "Item 2",
    "ncContentTypeAlias": "products",
    "categoryNumber": "02",
    "categoryHeading1": "Centreline and borrowpit",
    "categoryHeading2": "borrowpit",
    "category": "<p>Borrow pits are identified for the supply of material requirements for both general fill, gravel and aggregates. Borrow Pit areas can be remediated using unsuitable materials removed from the construction site. Hence the material excavated is ‘borrowed’.</p>",
    "categoryImage": "umb://media/baf84be0089c4a309ce39059c65745f3"
  },
  {
    "key": "7d3d0c08-29a3-4ffa-9f43-eb3747bc140c",
    "name": "Item 3",
    "ncContentTypeAlias": "products",
    "categoryNumber": "03",
    "categoryHeading1": "Road Pavement Evaluations",
    "categoryHeading2": "Evaluations",
    "category": "<div id=\"1\">\n<p>Appropriate pavement investigation is necessary to ensure the adequacy and cost efficiencies of the pavement design or remediation, and to avoid costly construction problems due to unforeseen variations in pavement/subgrade composition, stability and strength.</p>\n</div>",
    "categoryImage": "umb://media/4d451178365e48fc8173955a1bac9b6e"
  },
  {
    "key": "ff45d44e-86b9-4cd3-9bb0-57262438f034",
    "name": "Item 4",
    "ncContentTypeAlias": "products",
    "categoryNumber": "04",
    "categoryHeading1": "Site investigation",
    "categoryHeading2": "investigation",
    "category": "<p>Our teams are able to carry out soil and geotechnical investigations including sampling, profiling, testing and reporting. Such data is required to assist with foundation designs and other structural plans.</p>",
    "categoryImage": "umb://media/4ae29f11290346c0b480640f9c10d149"
  },
  {
    "key": "902c5244-fa69-46fb-8bdd-072fed49195e",
    "name": "Item 5",
    "ncContentTypeAlias": "products",
    "categoryNumber": "05",
    "categoryHeading1": "Drilling ",
    "categoryHeading2": "",
    "category": "<p>Geotechnical drilling is performed as part of the construction process. This is mainly for structures such as multi-storey buildings. A geotechnical engineer usually oversees the process to ensure that the drilling meets the requirements of the project.</p>",
    "categoryImage": "umb://media/957c05573d1645a9beeeeecf13064ed4"
  }
]]]></Value>
